title: 'statement-store: split the v2 inbound statement slots by peer role'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    With the v2 DHT path on, the statement set reserves only the peers that steering picks, every
    other peer holds an inbound slot and the protocol controller dials no peer of its own. Steering
    keeps up to `replication_factor` routing peers reserved besides the peers covering the node's
    topics: the nearest peer of every distance bucket, then the nearest peers overall. The set
    gets the node's light allowance on top of its inbound slots and the handler splits them by
    role, so a light peer is admitted while the full slots are taken. The full slots come from the
    new `--statement-in-peers` flag, 50 by default. `StatementHandlerPrototype::new` takes the
    network configuration and the v2 DHT configuration as new arguments.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
- name: staging-node-cli
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: major
